concept:australian-heritage-council-act-2003-sec-16 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "16 Who presides at meetings"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-16 ;
    values:originalText "(1) The Chair presides at all meetings at which he or she is present.  (2) If the Chair is not present at a meeting, the members present, other than associate members, may elect a member, other than an associate member, to preside at the meeting." ;
    skos:definition "(1) The Chair presides at all meetings at which he or she is present.  (2) If the Chair is not present at a meeting, the members present, other than associate members, may elect a member, other than an associate member, to preside at the meeting."@en ;
