concept:australian-heritage-council-act-2003-sec-18 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "18 Voting at meetings"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-18 ;
    values:originalText "(1) A question is decided by a majority of the votes of the members, other than associate members, present and voting.  (2) The person presiding at a meeting has a deliberative vote and, if necessary, also a casting vote." ;
    skos:definition "(1) A question is decided by a majority of the votes of the members, other than associate members, present and voting.  (2) The person presiding at a meeting has a deliberative vote and, if necessary, also a casting vote."@en ;
